					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-9081717#post-4112718</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-9081717/aces-and-eights#post-4112718</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Jan 2019 16:13:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>mayoculpa</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3489662</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I know there are a bunch of other folks also working on Aces &amp; Eights tales, and I wanted to share a couple of offsite resources that have been super helpful to me during the outlining process.</p> <p><a href="http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~poindexterfamily/genealogy/OldWestSlang.html">Old West Slang</a> &#8212; In addition to being a great list of authentic Old West phrases, it also has links to similarly useful pages like popular first names, horse facts, gun basics, and cowboy songs.</p> <p><a href="http://www.let.rug.nl/usa/essays/1801-1900/the-iron-horse/ideology.php">Ideology of Railroads</a> &#8212; This American history page includes short, informative essays about important political events in the 19th century, plus a bit of insight into the logistics and culture of the time.</p> <p>At this point I have way more ideas than it's humanly possible for me to write so uh, if you wanna do An8 brainstorming hmu. &gt;_&gt;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
