					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Heck, they weren't punished all that much in actual history. Johnson pardoned a lot of Confederates, didn't try a single one for treason and looked the other way when the former rebel states set up Jim Crow.</p> <p>Did the 13th, 14th and 15th Amendments still get passed?</p> 
				 	]]>
